@page "/AccessibilityStatement"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Accessibility statement";
    ViewData["PageTitle"] = "Accessibility statement";
}

<p class="govuk-body">
    We aim to make the Histopathology System easy to use for everyone. This service is designed to be
    accessible and compatible with the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 AA standard.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">How accessible this service is</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    We are working to ensure the service is accessible to all users, including people using assistive
    technologies. We test pages for keyboard access, focus styles, reading order, colour contrast,
    form labels, and responsive behaviour.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Known issues</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    We review any accessibility issues identified during testing and address them as part of ongoing service
    updates. If you experience a problem that is not listed here, please contact the service team.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Feedback and contact information</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    If you need information in a different format, or if you find a problem with the service, please email
    <a class="govuk-link" href="mailto:itu.helpdesk@apha.gov.uk">itu.helpdesk@apha.gov.uk</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Enforcement procedure</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
    If you are not satisfied with our response, you can contact the Equality Advisory and Support Service
    (EASS) or the Equality Commission for Northern Ireland (ECNI) as appropriate.
</p>

<p class="govuk-body">
    This statement was last reviewed on @DateTime.Today.ToString("d MMMM yyyy").
</p>
